title The module front doors too, and the rooms that keep the word on purpose
prompt publishing the seed now, then starting the loop
think Ran the leak gate before his hand reached it, so a refusal would arrive with its reason attached rather than as a surprise. SOW_WITNESS_GREEN, copied 6712, scrubbed 1032, withheld 122, IDENT_CLEAN and NO_PERSONAL both clean.
think Checked the seed allowlist for the rooms this day touched, since a room absent from it ships as invisible and that fault has landed twice. tools, foundations, context, docs-geode, manual, active-designing and active-development all ship; crux, session-logs and recursion-prompts are withheld, which is right -- the operator card, the logs and the loop prompts are internal surfaces.
think Then asked what the seed would still SAY after the republish, which found a gap in my own roster. Module rooms ship, and a newcomer browsing the repository meets caravan/README.md as surely as the manual, yet I had scoped the sweep to the documentation rooms alone.
think Read those before sweeping them and kept most of them. Ember's corpus is a term of art -- for an inference module's readers, training corpus IS the clearest word, and swapping it for collection would make the page less precise, which is exactly the abstract-for-abstract mistake this sweep was shaped to avoid. image's font5x7 corpora are glyph sets, mostly inside identifiers. Fixture files are inputs with expected outputs, so rewording one changes what a witness proves.
think Swept only what was doing a generic job: caravan's four occurrences, every one a witness control set, and scribble's single line, which means document work. Wrote the term-of-art exemptions into the scan's header as a decision rather than leaving them as an oversight.
obs The guard caught my own incomplete sweep twice in a row -- once at enforce_hits=1 after the first pass, once more after the second -- which is the argument for building it before the commit rather than after the drift, made on the same afternoon it was built.
obs Ran caravan's own copy witness after editing its README, since that file is long and load-bearing. GREEN.
loom leak_gate=green copied=6712 scrubbed=1032 withheld=122 seed_commits=1
loom enforce_files=339 enforce_hits=0 record_files=362 module_readmes_swept=2 term_of_art_kept=3
file caravan/README.md four witness control sets, named as what they are
file scribble/README.md document work rather than the borrowed noun
file tools/fixtures/vocabulary_collection_scan.sh the module front doors added, the term-of-art rooms named
recommend check-in (Keaton) the leak gate is green and the front doors are clean, so the publish and the loop are both clear to run. If the seed went out before this commit landed, these two READMEs ride the next publish and nothing is broken either way.
